  "reason": "The current best is config_037 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.706). In the RNA-only setting, avgpool clearly outperformed transformer (0.591 vs 0.519), but that comparison was made without a strong image encoder. In the multimodal setting, the interaction between aggregation strategy and the VIT image features is untested. Config_039 is a single-variable extension of the best configuration, swapping avgpool for transformer while keeping all other settings identical. This directly tests whether transformer aggregation can better capture cross-profile and cross-modal interactions when paired with the richer VIT image representations. If it improves, we identify a new best; if it does not, we confirm avgpool as the optimal aggregation and can focus remaining budget on other dimensions. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information experiment because it resolves uncertainty on the last unexplored design axis of the current best configuration without introducing multiple confounding changes."
}

